  "timingNotes": "Note identity and boundaries come from a harmonic-sum f0 track (4096-point window, 10-20ms hop, 45-90 MIDI search at 0.05-semitone resolution) run over each section; onsets are then refined to the pick transient on a three-pole 5kHz-highpassed 1ms RMS envelope, searched backwards from each pitch-run start and backtracked to 30% of the attack peak. Three sections, all in one file: quarters 5580-11115ms (13 notes, measured 399-456ms apart, mean 423ms vs 428.6ms theoretical), eighths 14127-18231ms (18 notes, 180-250ms apart, mean 216ms vs 214.3ms), eighth-note triplets 24427-28090ms (24 notes, 90-188ms apart, mean 144ms vs 142.9ms). The played figure is A B C D C B repeated, not the B C D E D C the performer described: quarters run that six-note cell twice and then a closing A; eighths run it twice then A B C D E A; triplets run it three times then A B C D E A. Octaves confirmed against the spectrum (A4 440Hz, B4 494Hz, C5 523Hz, D5 587Hz, E5 659Hz). The 26.0s B4 in the triplet section is quiet enough that a transient-only detector misses it, but the f0 track holds B4 for four frames there and the surrounding intervals are 137ms and 143ms, so it is a played note. No detector output was used to derive any value here.",
